<title>USA: IES Utilities Iowa power plant restarts.</title>
<headline>IES Utilities Iowa power plant restarts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>IES Utilities Inc's 212 megawatt coal-fired power station in Burlington, Iowa resumed electrical output on Sunday following a scheduled maintenance outage, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The plant was shut Oct 4 for the maintenance in preparation for winter season, spokeswoman Diane Ramsey said Monday.</p>
<p>The Burlington station is wholly-owned and operated by IES Utilities, which is based in Cedar Rapids, Iowa.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
